1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,540
Every company runs on processes,

2
00:00:02,560 --> 00:00:04,940
and on the guides that explain them.

3
00:00:04,960 --> 00:00:07,500
For our finance teams, those guides are

4
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:09,020
the PGs.

5
00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:12,860
The day D365 changes, they start going out

6
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:13,900
of date.

7
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:15,820
In a big transformation,

8
00:00:15,840 --> 00:00:18,380
people get trained, documents get built

9
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:20,300
and recordings get stored,

10
00:00:20,320 --> 00:00:23,340
and then it all slowly goes out of date,

11
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:25,340
because it's hard to maintain.

12
00:00:25,360 --> 00:00:29,340
Every D365 update, new module and rollout

13
00:00:29,360 --> 00:00:31,180
wave is another round.

14
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:33,980
Each one sends the team back to re-shoot,

15
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:36,810
rewrite and re-translate the PGs,

16
00:00:36,960 --> 00:00:38,300
by hand.

17
00:00:38,320 --> 00:00:41,340
And the PGs are Ava's source of truth in

18
00:00:41,360 --> 00:00:44,140
Teams, so when a PG is out of date,

19
00:00:44,160 --> 00:00:46,380
so are Ava's answers.

20
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:48,940
The PG Builder turns recordings,

21
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:51,980
manuals and other material into PGs to the

22
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:53,900
current approved standard.

23
00:00:53,920 --> 00:00:56,460
System Replay, the third use case,

24
00:00:56,480 --> 00:01:00,220
checks those PGs against D365 and feeds

25
00:01:00,240 --> 00:01:02,830
what it finds back into them.

26
00:01:02,850 --> 00:01:05,950
It starts from a PG the team already has.

27
00:01:05,970 --> 00:01:08,990
The author walks through it once in D365

28
00:01:09,010 --> 00:01:10,510
with the browser extension,

29
00:01:10,530 --> 00:01:12,830
which ties each step to the real button

30
00:01:12,850 --> 00:01:14,030
or field.

31
00:01:14,050 --> 00:01:17,070
From then on, it can replay the whole PG

32
00:01:17,090 --> 00:01:18,030
on its own.

33
00:01:18,050 --> 00:01:20,590
Each button or field is recorded several

34
00:01:20,610 --> 00:01:21,230
ways:

35
00:01:21,250 --> 00:01:23,790
its ID, its role and name,

36
00:01:23,810 --> 00:01:26,670
its label, and its place on the page.

37
00:01:26,690 --> 00:01:28,350
If the first check fails,

38
00:01:28,370 --> 00:01:29,950
it moves on to the next,

39
00:01:29,970 --> 00:01:33,340
so a button that has moved is still found.

40
00:01:33,410 --> 00:01:37,150
After a D365 update, that replay becomes

41
00:01:37,170 --> 00:01:39,550
a PG versus system check.

42
00:01:39,570 --> 00:01:42,830
Steps that don't match are flagged as discrepancies,

43
00:01:42,850 --> 00:01:45,150
and the author decides which is right:

44
00:01:45,170 --> 00:01:47,470
the system or the PG.

45
00:01:47,490 --> 00:01:49,550
If the PG needs to change,

46
00:01:49,570 --> 00:01:51,870
the plan is to pass the confirmed change

47
00:01:51,890 --> 00:01:54,590
to the PG Builder, so the update follows

48
00:01:54,610 --> 00:01:56,910
its rules and goes through the usual review

49
00:01:56,930 --> 00:01:58,140
and sign-off.

50
00:01:58,460 --> 00:02:01,000
Every run also captures a fresh,

51
00:02:01,020 --> 00:02:03,480
highlighted screenshot of each step,

52
00:02:03,500 --> 00:02:05,560
ready for the PG when it needs one,

53
00:02:05,580 --> 00:02:07,240
to support an audit trail,

54
00:02:07,260 --> 00:02:09,800
or for any other training material.

55
00:02:09,820 --> 00:02:13,480
For Wave 2 and Wave 3, it can replay a PG

56
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:16,360
with D365 in another language.

57
00:02:16,380 --> 00:02:18,520
Nothing is machine-translated.

58
00:02:18,540 --> 00:02:22,280
It reads the exact label D365 shows on every

59
00:02:22,300 --> 00:02:24,920
button and field, and builds the localized

60
00:02:24,940 --> 00:02:26,920
documentation from those.

61
00:02:26,940 --> 00:02:29,720
The same steps and screenshots become training

62
00:02:29,740 --> 00:02:30,440
material:

63
00:02:30,460 --> 00:02:33,400
PowerPoint decks, a narrated walkthrough,

64
00:02:33,420 --> 00:02:36,440
practice, a short test and video clips.

65
00:02:36,460 --> 00:02:40,040
And a PG can sit on top of D365 itself,

66
00:02:40,060 --> 00:02:42,600
with Guide me highlighting each field and

67
00:02:42,620 --> 00:02:45,000
taking the user through the task one step

68
00:02:45,020 --> 00:02:45,960
at a time.

69
00:02:45,980 --> 00:02:48,920
Authors can also record a new process straight

70
00:02:48,940 --> 00:02:50,440
into System Replay.

71
00:02:50,460 --> 00:02:52,920
They do the task in D365,

72
00:02:52,940 --> 00:02:55,000
the steps and screenshots are written for

73
00:02:55,020 --> 00:02:57,480
them, and it shows up in the extension straight

74
00:02:57,500 --> 00:02:59,830
away for anyone on that screen.

75
00:02:59,850 --> 00:03:03,110
Each process already exports as a Word document.

76
00:03:03,130 --> 00:03:05,910
The next idea is to attach the PG Builder

77
00:03:05,930 --> 00:03:08,150
to that, so one recording could produce

78
00:03:08,170 --> 00:03:11,270
the PG itself, in full or in part.

79
00:03:11,290 --> 00:03:14,470
That's a work in progress and isn't guaranteed.

80
00:03:14,490 --> 00:03:17,190
Part of the recent AI spend went into building

81
00:03:17,210 --> 00:03:18,310
System Replay.

82
00:03:18,330 --> 00:03:20,150
Running it uses none.

83
00:03:20,170 --> 00:03:22,870
Replays, checks and screenshots run on their

84
00:03:22,890 --> 00:03:26,390
own, so using it more adds no AI spend.

85
00:03:26,410 --> 00:03:29,110
It runs as a single container on a dedicated

86
00:03:29,130 --> 00:03:31,430
server, and authors sign in with an access

87
00:03:31,450 --> 00:03:32,070
key.

88
00:03:32,090 --> 00:03:34,550
The extension only talks to that server,

89
00:03:34,570 --> 00:03:36,790
so PG content stays on it.

90
00:03:36,810 --> 00:03:38,950
Today it's a working prototype,

91
00:03:38,970 --> 00:03:41,110
built and tested on a demo app.

92
00:03:41,130 --> 00:03:43,190
It still needs a lot of work before it's

93
00:03:43,210 --> 00:03:44,230
ready for the business,

94
00:03:44,250 --> 00:03:46,550
and the PG Builder comes first.

95
00:03:46,570 --> 00:03:48,790
The PG stays the output.

96
00:03:48,810 --> 00:03:50,870
System Replay keeps the PGs,

97
00:03:50,890 --> 00:03:53,830
and Ava, current, and gets more from them:

98
00:03:53,850 --> 00:03:56,550
screenshots, localized documentation,

99
00:03:56,570 --> 00:03:59,780
training and help inside D365.
